.Dd June 9, 2026
.Dt MBT_LOG 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_log_set ,
.Nm mbt_log_set_debug ,
.Nm mbt_log_stderr ,
.Nm mbt_log_syslog ,
.Nm mbt_log_level_str ,
.Nm mbt_log_component_str ,
.Nm mbt_log_emit
.Nd BitTorrent logging utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/log.h
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_log_set "mbt_log_fn fn" "void *arg"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_log_set_debug "uint32_t component_mask"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_log_stderr "enum mbt_log_level level" "enum mbt_log_component comp" "const char *fmt" "va_list ap" "void *arg"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_log_syslog "enum mbt_log_level level" "enum mbt_log_component comp" "const char *fmt" "va_list ap" "void *arg"
.Ft const char *
.Fn mbt_log_level_str "enum mbt_log_level level"
.Ft const char *
.Fn mbt_log_component_str "enum mbt_log_component comp"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_log_emit "enum mbt_log_level level" "enum mbt_log_component comp" "const char *fmt" "..."
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The logging module provides a structured logging system for the library.
Logs are categorized by level and component.
.Pp
.Sh Log Levels
The
.Fa mbt_log_level
enumeration defines the severity of the log:
.Bl -tag -width on_level
.It MBT_LOG_ERROR
Fatal errors.
.It MBT_LOG_WARN
Warnings and potential issues.
.It MBT_LOG_INFO
Informational messages about normal operation.
.It MBT_LOG_DEBUG
Fine-grained debugging information.
.El
.Pp
.Sh Log Components
The
.Fa mbt_log_component
enumeration defines the source of the log using a bitmask:
.Bl -tag -width on_comp
.It MBT_LOG_SESSION
Session management.
.It MBT_LOG_TORRENT
Torrent operations.
.It MBT_LOG_PEER
Peer interaction.
.It MBT_LOG_CONN
Connection/Network events.
.It MBT_LOG_LSD
Local Service Discovery.
.It MBT_LOG_DHT
Distributed Hash Table.
.It MBT_LOG_STORAGE
Storage operations.
.It MBT_LOG_PICKER
Piece picking logic.
.It MBT_LOG_TRACKER
Tracker client interaction.
.It MBT_LOG_TRACKERD
Tracker server logic.
.It MBT_LOG_ALL
All components (0x7FFFFFFF).
.El
.Pp
.Sh Functions
.Fn mbt_log_set
registers a custom log callback function. This function will be invoked
whenever a log event is emitted. If
.Fa fn
is
.Fa NULL, logging is disabled by default.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_log_set_debug
enables debug-level logging for specific components. The
.Fa component_mask
is a bitmask of
.Fa mbt_log_component
values. By default, no components emit debug messages unless explicitly set here.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_log_stderr
and
.Fn mbt_log_syslog
are built-in callback implementations that write logs to standard error or
system logger, respectively.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_log_level_str
and
.Fn mbt_log_component_str
return a human-readable string representation of the level and component.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_log_emit
is used to emit log messages at a specific level and component. It is primarily
used by the convenience macros, but can be called directly.
.Sh Macros
The following macros are used throughout the library to simplify logging at
designated levels. They all take an
.Fa mbt_log_component
as the first argument, followed by a format string and variadic arguments:
.Bl -tag -width on_macro
.It mbt_log_error(comp, ...)
Logs an error message with component
.Fa comp .
.It mbt_log_warn(comp, ...)
Logs a warning message with component
.Fa comp .
.It mbt_log_info(comp, ...)
Logs an info message with component
.Fa comp .
.It mbt_log_debug(comp, ...)
Logs a debug message with component
.Fa comp .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_session 3
